- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/flip.html
- Summary (EN): The Flip node mirrors a layer across the horizontal, vertical, or diagonal axis of image space, and these transformations can be combined. Its Mask parameter controls how much of the flipped result replaces the original.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Flip retourne une couche horizontalement, verticalement ou en diagonale, avec un mélange réglable par masque.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: original layer to flip", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask whose strength is scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Mask: how much of the flipped value mixes with the original; default 1 uses only the flipped result", "Flip Horizontally: flips the layer about the y-axis", "Flip Vertically: flips the layer about the x-axis", "Flip Diagonally: flips diagonally and swaps the resolution, for example 1920x1080 becomes 1080x1920"]

- Caveats: ["A diagonal flip changes the resolution and aspect ratio, so the width and height of a non-square layer are swapped"]

